{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00542",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.87,
      "end_seconds": 10.45,
      "duration_seconds": 9.58,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got numbness in my right hand and it's really scaring me. I keep thinking it's a stroke, or my spine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.98,
      "end_seconds": 16.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "Righto, let's sort it out. Which fingers are numb?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.37,
      "end_seconds": 30.22,
      "duration_seconds": 11.85,
      "text": "The thumb, the pointer finger and the middle one. Not the little finger. And it's worse when I'm gripping something, like the steering wheel."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.79,
      "end_seconds": 36.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "How long has it been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.88,
      "end_seconds": 38.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "About two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.29,
      "end_seconds": 43.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Does it do anything else, besides numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.55,
      "end_seconds": 61.66,
      "duration_seconds": 17.11,
      "text": "Tingling at night, like pins and needles. It wakes me up and I have to shake my hand out. And I've been dropping things, my coffee mug, a screwdriver last week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.74,
      "end_seconds": 64.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Any pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.33,
      "end_seconds": 79.76,
      "duration_seconds": 10.43,
      "text": "A sore ache in the wrist, and sometimes it runs up the forearm. Shaking it out helps a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.35,
      "end_seconds": 84.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Okay. Any pain in your neck?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.75,
      "end_seconds": 88.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "No, no neck pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.75,
      "end_seconds": 92.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Any fall or injury to the wrist?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.89,
      "end_seconds": 95.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.65,
      "end_seconds": 100.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Any swelling in the wrist or hand?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.79,
      "end_seconds": 106.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "No, not that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.23,
      "end_seconds": 110.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Any weight loss lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.66,
      "end_seconds": 118.05,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "No, my weight's been steady. If anything it's gone up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.54,
      "end_seconds": 123.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "What do you do for work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.31,
      "end_seconds": 135.21,
      "duration_seconds": 8.9,
      "text": "I work on a production line, packing parts, same movement all day with a scanner gun."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.71,
      "end_seconds": 141.81,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "We'll come to that. What medicines are you on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.43,
      "end_seconds": 154.63,
      "duration_seconds": 11.2,
      "text": "Metformin, 500 mg twice a day, for the diabetes. Every day, never miss. Well, mostly. The evening one I sometimes forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.32,
      "end_seconds": 159.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Fair enough. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.08,
      "end_seconds": 173.64,
      "duration_seconds": 13.56,
      "text": "There's a small white tablet for my cholesterol, I take it at night. I can't remember the name of it, my wife keeps the box."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.54,
      "end_seconds": 178.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Okay. Do you have any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.6,
      "end_seconds": 188.89,
      "duration_seconds": 8.29,
      "text": "Penicillin. I was told as a kid I'm allergic to it, but I honestly don't remember what happened."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.55,
      "end_seconds": 197.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "Fine, I'll note it down. What other conditions have you got?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.97,
      "end_seconds": 213.33,
      "duration_seconds": 14.36,
      "text": "Type 2 diabetes, about six years. High cholesterol. Gout, though I haven't had a flare this year. And sleep apnoea, I use a machine at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.78,
      "end_seconds": 217.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Good. Any operations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.54,
      "end_seconds": 223.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "A hernia repair, about eight years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.49,
      "end_seconds": 228.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Family history of anything important?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.42,
      "end_seconds": 240.79,
      "duration_seconds": 10.37,
      "text": "My father had a heart attack at sixty. And my sister has carpal tunnel syndrome, she's a hairdresser."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.97,
      "end_seconds": 246.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Interesting. Do you smoke or drink?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.73,
      "end_seconds": 255.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.72,
      "text": "I quit smoking five years ago. And I have two beers on the weekend, no more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.12,
      "end_seconds": 259.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Do you exercise at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.83,
      "end_seconds": 268.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.83,
      "text": "I walk the dog on Sundays. That's about it, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.48,
      "end_seconds": 272.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Alright. Any chest pain or palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 273.2,
      "end_seconds": 275.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "No, my heart feels fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.24,
      "end_seconds": 282.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "And passing urine, any trouble there, more than usual?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.49,
      "end_seconds": 288.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "No, that's normal. I'm drinking the same as always."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.22,
      "end_seconds": 305.68,
      "duration_seconds": 7.46,
      "text": "Let me check your numbers. Blood pressure is 136 over 84, pulse is 80 beats per minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.91,
      "end_seconds": 322.02,
      "duration_seconds": 9.11,
      "text": "Hands out, palms up. I'll tap over the wrist crease here. Tell me what you feel."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.45,
      "end_seconds": 330.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "Ow, tingling shoots into my fingers. That's exactly the feeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.86,
      "end_seconds": 349.58,
      "duration_seconds": 12.72,
      "text": "The tapping over the wrist brings on the tingling. Now push the backs of your hands together, wrists bent, and hold for a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 351.44,
      "end_seconds": 356.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "It's coming on already. Pins and needles in the same three fingers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.58,
      "end_seconds": 374.09,
      "duration_seconds": 9.51,
      "text": "Yep. Bending the wrist like that brings on the same tingling. Now light touch on each fingertip, eyes closed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 375.18,
      "end_seconds": 381.71,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "It's duller on the thumb and the first two fingers. The little finger feels normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.03,
      "end_seconds": 398.56,
      "duration_seconds": 10.53,
      "text": "Reduced feeling in the thumb, index and middle fingers, then. And squeeze my fingers as hard as you can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 400.49,
      "end_seconds": 403.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Like this? It doesn't feel strong."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 405.99,
      "end_seconds": 420.39,
      "duration_seconds": 14.4,
      "text": "Grip is a little weaker on the right than the left. Based on all this, it looks like carpal tunnel syndrome, where a nerve gets squeezed in the wrist."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 422.69,
      "end_seconds": 427.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "So it's not a stroke? Or my spine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 428.9,
      "end_seconds": 434.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "Nothing here points to either. Your job could well be the trigger."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 436.62,
      "end_seconds": 440.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "What do we do about it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 441.68,
      "end_seconds": 454.12,
      "duration_seconds": 12.44,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a nerve conduction study, to measure how well the nerve is working. And a blood test for your HbA1c, to check your sugar control."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 456.38,
      "end_seconds": 460.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Okay. And if the nerve test is normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 462.94,
      "end_seconds": 471.02,
      "duration_seconds": 8.08,
      "text": "Then I might consider an X-ray of your neck, but we'll hold off on that for now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 472.81,
      "end_seconds": 481.7,
      "duration_seconds": 8.89,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got a wrist splint in the right size here. Shall I show him how to put it on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 483.39,
      "end_seconds": 497.07,
      "duration_seconds": 13.68,
      "text": "Please do. Wear it at night, so the wrist stays straight while you sleep. And take short breaks from the scanner gun during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 499.04,
      "end_seconds": 505.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.97,
      "text": "I'll do it, and I'll tell my supervisor. And the follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 507.34,
      "end_seconds": 518.81,
      "duration_seconds": 11.47,
      "text": "Come back if it's not better in four weeks, and bring the tablet box this time so we can get its name."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 519.72,
      "end_seconds": 525.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "Right, my wife will find it. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}
